<b>Belt</b>

03:34.260 --> 03:38.360
The fact that they're kind of into it 
somehow makes it even worse.

03:38.360 --> 03:42.560
Huh? Seems like you have 
to pick it up yourself.

03:42.560 --> 03:44.620
And look at this.

03:44.620 --> 03:49.870
<b>Order</b>

03:44.620 --> 03:49.870
<b>When picking up 
your order, 
a compatibility test 
will be conducted. 
-Hata</b>

03:45.160 --> 03:49.870
It says, "When picking up your order, 
a compatibility test will be conducted."

03:50.120 --> 03:51.530
A compatibility test?

03:52.420 --> 03:55.190
I'm givin' you a test!

03:58.230 --> 04:00.500
No turning back now.

04:04.670 --> 04:07.210
Hyoma-chan, you finally made it!

04:07.210 --> 04:09.280
Haven't seen you since the Sogenbi thing!

04:09.280 --> 04:11.340
Hey, how's the leg?

04:11.340 --> 04:13.080
Hyoma...chan?

04:13.080 --> 04:14.020
What brings you here?

04:14.020 --> 04:16.780
I ordered new clothes, too!

04:16.780 --> 04:19.530
I heard you'd be coming, so I hung around!

04:19.530 --> 04:21.450
Plus you didn't text or call!

04:21.450 --> 04:22.830
Well, I didn't have any news—

04:22.830 --> 04:24.880
Do it anyway!

04:24.880 --> 04:25.980
Excuse me!

04:25.980 --> 04:28.410
Do you two... know each other?

04:28.700 --> 04:31.220
Yes, she's...

04:31.700 --> 04:33.980
Could you please give me some space?

04:32.660 --> 04:34.460
Oh, you!

04:35.400 --> 04:39.520
She's one of the Saenome 
policing the tsukumogami in Kyoto.

04:39.520 --> 04:42.550
Kadomori Tsubaki. We're colleagues.

04:42.550 --> 04:44.680
Oh, thank you for your service.

04:44.680 --> 04:45.480
I'm Naga—

04:45.480 --> 04:46.540
I know who you are.

04:46.540 --> 04:47.550
Botan-chan.

04:48.160 --> 04:51.560
I know <i>all</i> about the Nagatsukis from work.

04:53.760 --> 04:58.390
Hey, Botan-chan. Are you...

04:59.940 --> 05:02.000
Hyoma-chan's girlfriend?!

05:02.000 --> 05:03.570
Why are all of you like this?!

05:03.900 --> 05:06.030
That reaction just seals the deal!

05:06.030 --> 05:06.880
No—

05:06.030 --> 05:08.570
It's really not like that, Kadomori-san!

05:08.570 --> 05:10.840
Hey, call me Tsubaki.

05:10.840 --> 05:12.700
Nice to meet you, Botan-chan.

05:18.530 --> 05:20.300
Anyway, it's on the second floor.

05:20.300 --> 05:21.180
This way.

05:23.670 --> 05:27.070
Tsubaki-san's very easygoing, isn't she?

05:27.070 --> 05:29.100
She does march to her own drumbeat.

05:29.100 --> 05:30.970
Though she is quite skilled.

05:39.010 --> 05:42.230
Tsubaki, are you aware of the "test"?

05:42.230 --> 05:46.430
Yeah. It's not especially hard...

05:46.430 --> 05:48.740
Though I don't know how it'll be for you.

05:49.760 --> 05:50.740
What do you mean by that?

05:50.740 --> 05:54.330
<b>Tebata
Fabrics</b>

05:51.120 --> 05:53.110
It's kind of a special thing.

05:55.000 --> 05:56.090
Cloth?

05:57.420 --> 06:00.000
Wh-What's going on?!

06:00.000 --> 06:00.880
Botan!

06:01.370 --> 06:02.350
Are you all right?

06:02.350 --> 06:03.930
Y-Yeah.

06:03.930 --> 06:06.330
It's actually quite soft, but...

06:06.330 --> 06:08.130
Sorry 'bout that!

06:08.130 --> 06:11.580
The cloth we make here 
has some special properties.

06:11.580 --> 06:13.760
It's got a life of its own, you could say.

06:14.280 --> 06:16.920
A spinning wheel tsukumogami 
spins the thread,

06:16.770 --> 06:22.770
<b>— Hata —</b>

06:16.920 --> 06:20.230
and I, a hand loom tsukumogami, 
weave it together.

06:20.760 --> 06:23.500
Our nature kind of rubs off on it, I guess...

06:23.500 --> 06:24.150
Hey!

06:24.150 --> 06:27.070
Are you Nagatsuki Botan, dearie?

06:27.070 --> 06:28.680
Oh... hello.

06:28.680 --> 06:31.640
Well, no wonder it took such a shine to you!

06:31.640 --> 06:34.090
Never thought I'd see you 
in the flesh like this!

06:34.090 --> 06:35.630
Hang on, Hata!

06:35.630 --> 06:38.120
<i>We're</i> the customers here, remember?

06:38.120 --> 06:39.210
Oh, you bet!

06:39.210 --> 06:41.640
You know I'd never forget that!

06:40.880 --> 06:43.050
<i>Clothing created by tsukumogami...</i>

06:43.790 --> 06:47.050
The cloth itself isn't 
a tsukumogami, of course.

06:47.050 --> 06:49.930
It just picks up our 
transformative properties,

06:50.340 --> 06:55.930
so it can adjust endurance and flexibility 
in accordance with the wearer's will.

06:55.930 --> 06:58.080
"Living clothing."

06:58.080 --> 07:00.440
The "living" part is the key.

07:00.720 --> 07:02.650
You've gotta build a relationship with it,

07:02.650 --> 07:05.190
or it'll be uncooperative.

07:05.770 --> 07:08.030
Here, this one's done.

07:08.030 --> 07:08.940
For you, Tsubaki-san.

07:11.080 --> 07:13.200
Can you wear it to its full potential?

07:14.880 --> 07:16.790
That's the test.

07:17.770 --> 07:20.000
You really are good at that, eh?

07:20.000 --> 07:21.960
Well, I do it often enough.

07:21.960 --> 07:23.460
Amazing!

07:24.690 --> 07:25.960
Hyoma-san?

07:25.960 --> 07:30.700
Tsukumogami... all over my body. 
Tsukumogami... all over my body.

07:28.480 --> 07:31.470
I told you, it's not really a tsukumogami.

07:31.880 --> 07:33.720
Maybe you'd better not.

07:45.830 --> 07:49.790
It's all right. This is 
surely part of my training.

07:49.790 --> 07:50.780
Besides...

07:51.640 --> 07:55.870
Reducing my rate of injury will help 
to set your mind at ease, Botan.

07:56.390 --> 07:57.800
Hyoma-san...

08:02.580 --> 08:04.590
Very well. I accept your challenge.

08:04.590 --> 08:05.750
That's the spirit.

08:06.060 --> 08:09.200
Of course, there are many 
kinds of relationships.

08:09.200 --> 08:11.690
Friendly relationships, 
master-servant relationships...

08:11.690 --> 08:16.260
The key is just convincing it 
that you're a worthy wearer.

08:20.770 --> 08:22.590
A staredown, huh?

08:22.590 --> 08:24.860
A very strained atmosphere.

08:24.860 --> 08:27.210
Not exactly a great start.

08:27.210 --> 08:29.800
But it latched right on to me...

08:29.800 --> 08:31.050
You're a rare case.

08:31.050 --> 08:34.080
Yep, they're not so friendly with most.

08:34.080 --> 08:35.280
Really?

08:35.710 --> 08:38.110
Same with the others in your household.

08:38.110 --> 08:42.160
You're capable of building some 
pretty unprecedented relationships.

08:42.600 --> 08:44.300
I am?

08:46.000 --> 08:48.040
<i>And that's just one part</i>

08:48.520 --> 08:52.650
<i>of why Papa finds you 
so very, very dangerous.</i>

08:53.560 --> 08:55.790
What will Hyoma-san do, then?

08:55.790 --> 08:58.050
Probably what we all do.

08:58.410 --> 08:59.560
Discipline!

08:59.560 --> 09:01.980
Dominate it through sheer force, 
bring it to heel,

09:01.980 --> 09:03.930
and forge a master-servant relationship.

09:04.640 --> 09:05.940
You force it, then?

09:06.810 --> 09:11.820
Hyoma-chan probably sees that 
as his ideal method, too.

09:12.440 --> 09:14.070
You think so?

09:14.600 --> 09:17.530
It might have been that way 
when he first came to us,

09:18.010 --> 09:22.490
but I feel like he might find 
a different solution now.

09:25.440 --> 09:27.360
Well, let's get fighting.

09:27.360 --> 09:28.540
Huh?! No way!

09:29.470 --> 09:31.210
Let's not beat around the bush.

09:31.210 --> 09:32.970
Give me your best shot 
with all the power you have.

09:33.400 --> 09:35.550
Let's see if we can trust 
each other with our lives...

09:35.980 --> 09:37.550
through use of fists!

09:39.650 --> 09:41.100
What in the world?

09:41.100 --> 09:44.270
They don't even understand 
the spoken word, do they?

09:44.270 --> 09:46.320
No, they don't.

09:46.320 --> 09:49.510
But it looks like the sentiment got through.

09:53.320 --> 09:54.320
Begin!

10:02.200 --> 10:03.330
Hyoma-san!

10:06.110 --> 10:07.840
No need to worry.

10:07.840 --> 10:10.470
I'm stronger than this.

10:10.470 --> 10:12.310
I'm sure you can see that, as well.

10:15.340 --> 10:16.340
Good.

10:17.720 --> 10:19.720
Now it's my turn!

10:26.390 --> 10:27.420
Huh?!

10:27.420 --> 10:29.390
It's <i>that</i> kind of thing?!

10:29.740 --> 10:33.080
I'm impressed that you 
endured my full-force strike.

10:33.080 --> 10:36.530
I feel I could entrust my life 
to you as my armor.

10:37.050 --> 10:38.510
As reticent as I might be about it,

10:38.510 --> 10:41.220
I require your service for the fight ahead.

10:41.680 --> 10:45.370
I swear I will wear you well, wear you out,

10:45.370 --> 10:48.860
and allow you to fulfill the purpose 
for which you were born.

10:48.860 --> 10:50.170
Join me!

10:50.680 --> 10:52.280
We have a common interest.

10:52.280 --> 10:54.390
Our relationship is that of comrades in arms!

10:55.230 --> 10:58.730
Was that it? He wasn't just resorting to force?

10:59.960 --> 11:01.930
It's a gray area, I guess,

11:02.250 --> 11:04.930
but the cloth seems pretty satisfied, so...

11:05.440 --> 11:06.800
I guess all's well that ends well.

11:12.190 --> 11:15.190
<b>Tebata Fabrics</b>

11:15.600 --> 11:16.890
I'm sorry for the wait.

11:17.400 --> 11:18.590
No problem.

11:18.590 --> 11:21.960
Hey... You don't look any different.

11:21.960 --> 11:23.370
It seems not.

11:23.370 --> 11:26.080
It even transformed to match 
my outfit's color and form.

11:26.080 --> 11:27.230
And Tsubaki?

11:27.230 --> 11:28.720
She headed out already.

11:28.720 --> 11:30.080
I see.

11:31.590 --> 11:34.840
Hyoma-san, you seem pleased with yourself.

11:35.130 --> 11:36.140
You could tell?

11:36.140 --> 11:37.610
Yeah, kinda.

11:37.610 --> 11:40.340
I admit, I surprised myself today.

11:40.880 --> 11:43.920
I usually see tsukumogami 
as merely things to destroy,

11:43.920 --> 11:46.920
but today I looked one in the proverbial eye 
and reached an agreement with it.

11:48.420 --> 11:53.340
Quite frankly, I didn't think myself 
capable of such a thing.

11:54.460 --> 11:58.920
Perhaps I'm becoming the true 
Saenome that Grandfather spoke of.

12:00.020 --> 12:04.100
At the very least, I think you're 
heading in a good direction.

12:04.100 --> 12:05.620
I hope you're right.

12:06.360 --> 12:09.240
By the way, are you feeling fatigued?

12:09.240 --> 12:10.350
Could you tell?

12:10.350 --> 12:11.800
Vaguely.

12:11.800 --> 12:17.180
Well, while you were in there, 
it was just me and Tsubaki-san for a while.

12:17.180 --> 12:18.630
I see.

12:24.040 --> 12:25.640
Is that the Big Dipper?

12:26.140 --> 12:27.880
What a great hairpin.

12:27.880 --> 12:29.760
Oh... right.

12:29.760 --> 12:32.600
It really suits you. It's cute.

12:32.600 --> 12:33.890
Oh, well...

12:34.300 --> 12:37.320
Hyoma-chan's pretty cute too, huh?

12:41.320 --> 12:43.900
C-Cute? Him?

12:43.900 --> 12:47.570
Actually, I tried to make a move on him earlier...

12:47.570 --> 12:48.280
A mo—

12:48.280 --> 12:50.330
He blew me off, though.

12:50.330 --> 12:52.170
O-Oh...

12:52.590 --> 12:56.790
He's still too cute, though, 
so it's hard to back down.

13:00.820 --> 13:03.980
You're also very cute, and I like you, but...

13:04.890 --> 13:07.390
I-I wouldn't say I'm—

13:07.390 --> 13:08.810
I'm not losing to you.

13:12.420 --> 13:14.380
You truly do appear fatigued!

13:16.040 --> 13:19.940
So the kid managed to wear it, eh?

13:20.240 --> 13:23.770
But hey, nice of you to be tactful for once.

13:23.770 --> 13:25.160
You like Hyoma-chan now?

13:25.160 --> 13:26.360
Don't be dumb.

13:26.360 --> 13:28.950
Getting him the right equipment's 
just part of the rules.

13:29.230 --> 13:32.560
I also met the infamous Botan-chan.

13:32.560 --> 13:34.410
Super-cute girl.

13:34.410 --> 13:37.500
She and Hyoma-chan had a nice relationship.

13:37.500 --> 13:39.980
Lots of mutual trust there.

13:39.980 --> 13:41.290
Trust?

13:42.600 --> 13:43.800
I'd say, yeah.

13:44.710 --> 13:46.190
Strange.

13:46.190 --> 13:48.300
I'd met the girl once before, but...

13:49.330 --> 13:53.510
She didn't look like the type 
to open up to others at all.

13:54.400 --> 13:59.020
That's one reason I thought I could 
leave her at large a while longer.

13:59.960 --> 14:03.480
So that's a little unsettling to hear.

14:04.010 --> 14:09.000
Times like this, the strangest things 
start coming out of the woodwork.

14:10.980 --> 14:12.240
Hyoma-san!

14:12.240 --> 14:14.160
Could you lower the right side just a bit?

14:14.160 --> 14:15.360
Oh, just missed it!

14:15.360 --> 14:16.750
Now the left side's a little...

14:16.750 --> 14:18.750
<b>Hyakunin Isshu Society</b>

14:18.750 --> 14:20.750
<b>Hyakunin Isshu Society</b>

14:22.670 --> 14:23.800
Podium, check!

14:23.800 --> 14:25.200
Booklets, check!

14:25.200 --> 14:26.480
Sign, check!

14:26.480 --> 14:27.980
All ready to go!

14:27.980 --> 14:30.430
Boy, having a guy around speeds things up!

14:30.430 --> 14:32.460
Thanks for everything, Hyoma-san.

14:32.460 --> 14:33.580
It's nothing.

14:33.580 --> 14:36.180
The Hyakunin Isshu Society, is it?

14:36.720 --> 14:39.050
So you joined a club, as well?

14:39.050 --> 14:39.940
Actually,

14:40.190 --> 14:43.770
I did it all the time on New Year's 
at home, so I got pretty good at it.

14:44.490 --> 14:46.320
Don't you have classes?

14:46.320 --> 14:48.120
This is recruitment week.

14:47.690 --> 14:50.570
...and those are your 
recruiting stations. Let's do this!

14:48.120 --> 14:50.200
Classes pretty much don't start until Monday.

14:51.030 --> 14:53.160
Today's the day for nabbing new recruits!

14:53.160 --> 14:55.680
Here, Bon-chan, your share of the flyers.

14:55.680 --> 14:57.300
Oh, right!

14:58.240 --> 15:00.780
Kunato-san, thank you so much for your help.

15:00.780 --> 15:03.200
To be honest, when I first saw you,

15:03.200 --> 15:05.460
I assumed you were a bit of a hooligan.

15:05.790 --> 15:07.090
S-Senpai?!

15:07.090 --> 15:11.400
Yeah, at first I thought Nagatsuki-senpai 
had some underworld connections!

15:11.400 --> 15:12.400
Why?!

15:12.400 --> 15:14.000
Well, that glare...

15:14.000 --> 15:15.720
I feel like I should be begging for my life.

15:15.720 --> 15:18.060
But then it turned out 
he's such a hard worker...

15:18.060 --> 15:19.780
Secretly sensitive! So dreamy!

15:21.070 --> 15:22.670
We've got some time to kill,

15:22.670 --> 15:24.970
so why not take a campus tour...

15:24.970 --> 15:26.140
with your boyfriend.

15:26.140 --> 15:28.230
I told you, we're related!

15:28.720 --> 15:31.660
<i>She told them we're related?</i>

15:31.660 --> 15:32.740
<i>Speaking of which...</i>

15:33.320 --> 15:36.240
<i>What's </i>their<i> cover story?</i>

15:36.240 --> 15:40.360
Haori-san and the others 
are also your relatives, right?

15:40.360 --> 15:41.280
You've met the—

15:41.280 --> 15:43.910
Welp, here goes the tour!

15:45.260 --> 15:48.510
They came to my culture 
festival in my first year.

15:49.000 --> 15:51.790
My clubmates and classmates 
know all about them.

15:51.790 --> 15:53.980
Is that really safe?

15:53.980 --> 15:55.150
Seems like it.

15:55.150 --> 15:58.120
They just think we're a weird family, I guess.

15:58.120 --> 16:00.020
I wonder about that.

16:00.020 --> 16:01.550
Oh, I forgot.

16:01.550 --> 16:04.490
I've got a shift showing stuff to 
potential recruits this afternoon.

16:04.490 --> 16:06.150
There you are!

16:06.440 --> 16:07.400
Kao-chan!

16:07.400 --> 16:08.570
Botan!

16:09.000 --> 16:11.630
Could you help write a sign for us?

16:11.630 --> 16:12.450
Please, please!

16:12.450 --> 16:17.130
No worries, Hyoma-san! 
You can head back without me!

16:17.130 --> 16:18.830
R-Right.

16:19.540 --> 16:23.980
<i>Botan's life at school is 
livelier than I expected.</i>

16:25.790 --> 16:29.280
<i>But her tsukumogami, who came to her 
culture festival and generally enjoy revelry,</i>

16:29.280 --> 16:31.620
<i>didn't come with her today... curious.</i>

16:32.340 --> 16:34.170
First time in Kyoto, huh?

16:34.170 --> 16:36.340
I bet you wanna see everything, right?

16:36.640 --> 16:37.950
Just leave it to me!

16:37.950 --> 16:40.750
I've got my first-level 
Kyoto Tourism Certification.

16:40.750 --> 16:43.690
And I'm well-versed in everything 
from sweets to fast casual!

16:44.110 --> 16:48.460
So if you have any questions, 
just shoot me a line.

16:48.460 --> 16:49.860
Hey, Suzuri!

16:50.240 --> 16:52.860
Maybe you oughta focus a little.

16:52.860 --> 16:54.380
What's the big deal?

16:54.380 --> 16:56.350
Hyoma-kun's with her today.

16:56.350 --> 16:58.620
And if I can get a source on the inside here,

16:58.620 --> 17:01.670
it'll be a big help if anything 
goes down at her school.

17:01.670 --> 17:03.680
What about you, Nagi? What're you up to?

17:03.680 --> 17:07.210
I dropped in on the swordsmanship club 
and sliced through a training post.

17:07.660 --> 17:09.520
Sounds like you're the one 
who needs some focus.

17:09.520 --> 17:13.020
They called me "master," 
but I'm not cut out for teaching...

17:13.020 --> 17:15.610
Why are you picking up disciples?!

17:15.610 --> 17:17.720
You seem to be enjoying it, too.

17:18.440 --> 17:20.440
We don't want to stand out too much.

17:20.440 --> 17:21.720
Think it's time to head back?

17:21.720 --> 17:23.100
Good idea.

17:27.730 --> 17:29.100
Hang on a minute...

17:29.100 --> 17:29.730
Nagi?

17:30.280 --> 17:32.550
The hell's she doing here?

17:36.960 --> 17:37.740
Wait!

17:38.190 --> 17:41.160
<i>If that kid's here, that means...</i>

17:48.790 --> 17:50.500
You are called to battle...

17:51.780 --> 17:52.920
Kai-sama.

17:58.380 --> 18:00.850
An ambush? Here?!

18:02.440 --> 18:03.520
Would that be you?

18:05.190 --> 18:07.840
The new house guest at 
the Nagatsuki household...

18:07.840 --> 18:09.740
Kunato Hyoma?

18:10.960 --> 18:14.530
You look more frail than I expected.

18:23.400 --> 18:24.910
<i>The people disappeared...</i>

18:24.910 --> 18:26.900
<i>No, I'm in a barrier?</i>

18:28.160 --> 18:30.440
Now no one will interrupt.

18:31.040 --> 18:32.170
Now...

18:32.510 --> 18:36.170
Show me this reckless courage 
about which I've heard so much.

18:38.470 --> 18:40.540
Who exactly are you?

18:41.020 --> 18:44.910
No... it doesn't matter who you are, 
or what your reasons are.

18:44.910 --> 18:49.190
I can't leave at large any tsukumogami 
that turns its power on others.

18:49.600 --> 18:50.480
Let us begin.

18:50.480 --> 18:52.440
I'll finish you here and now!

18:53.410 --> 18:54.690
Go on and try.

18:58.030 --> 18:59.610
Here, you see it—

18:59.010 --> 18:59.860
There!

18:59.610 --> 19:01.480
The place where all people meet...

19:00.950 --> 19:01.930
So fast!

19:01.480 --> 19:04.600
Comers and goers...

19:01.930 --> 19:04.200
You can get that good in time.

19:04.200 --> 19:06.700
What do you think, new blood?

19:07.650 --> 19:10.500
<i>I wonder if Hyoma-san left.</i>

19:12.000 --> 19:14.710
<i>I wish he'd come by to play a bit.</i>

19:15.190 --> 19:18.660
<i>I just hope he hasn't gotten himself 
mixed up in something again.</i>

19:26.020 --> 19:27.640
<i>I feel so light...</i>

19:27.640 --> 19:29.050
<i>Is it the clothing?</i>

19:36.550 --> 19:37.780
<i>My strength, too...</i>

19:38.110 --> 19:41.370
<i>Of course. No wonder the 
Kyoto Saenome treasure it.</i>

19:42.150 --> 19:43.030
<i>But...</i>

19:43.600 --> 19:45.030
<i>Swords, spears...</i>

19:45.320 --> 19:48.040
<i>These planks are like the shoulder 
guards of Japanese armor.</i>

19:48.480 --> 19:51.290
<i>Typically, a tsukumogami's 
transformation powers</i>

19:51.290 --> 19:54.010
<i>are based on the one item 
they took as their vessel.</i>

19:55.140 --> 19:57.450
<i>But I've heard there are exceptions—</i>

19:57.450 --> 20:02.760
<i>tsukumogami that take a full 
"set" of items as their vessel.</i>

20:03.500 --> 20:04.440
<i>Could it be?</i>

20:06.310 --> 20:07.380
<i>Is he...</i>

20:08.700 --> 20:09.900
You're an absolute monster.

20:33.580 --> 20:34.580
Too soft.

20:37.400 --> 20:39.420
Th-The helmet?!

20:44.310 --> 20:47.680
Oh? That should've gone in deep...

20:47.960 --> 20:50.930
Yet no external injuries. 
That's excellent armor you've got.

20:51.280 --> 20:53.780
<i>Though it can't fully deflect 
the force of impact.</i>

20:57.300 --> 20:59.150
<i>I knew it.</i>

20:59.150 --> 21:02.820
<i>He's one of the three great 
tsukumogami of Kyoto...</i>

21:04.360 --> 21:06.300
<i>Kai, the suit of armor!</i>

21:07.730 --> 21:10.830
Hey, what brings you here?

21:11.330 --> 21:14.700
Shouldn't you be shut away, Itsuki?

21:16.460 --> 21:20.140
But the real problem is, 
I know you don't act alone.

21:20.140 --> 21:21.840
Where the hell is Kai?

21:22.330 --> 21:28.590
Kai-sama is meeting with Kunato Hyoma 
within the sanctuary I created.

21:28.880 --> 21:29.900
With Hyoma?!

21:29.900 --> 21:31.600
What? Why?!

21:32.560 --> 21:36.720
But this has all been disappointingly boring.

21:36.720 --> 21:39.110
Is this really all you have?

21:40.060 --> 21:41.670
What a shame.

21:43.650 --> 21:44.890
I might kill you.

21:45.830 --> 21:48.180
Kai-sama is engaged in his amusements.

21:48.670 --> 21:50.740
If you seek to intervene,

21:51.510 --> 21:53.640
you will have to go through me.

23:25.000 --> 23:40.020
<b>Next Time</b>

23:25.000 --> 23:40.020
<b>Efflorescence</b>
